# 0010. Plugins live in /opt/archminimal/plugins, set in each tool's config

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-18

Plugins, language servers and parsers that zsh, tmux and nvim download go to
`/opt/archminimal/plugins/<tool>` instead of `~/.local/share`. Each tool's config names that path
directly, so wiping home costs nothing, not even a re-download. Follows
[0007](0007-repos-live-in-opt-archminimal.adr).

## Technical details
- **Problem**: after 0007 the configs live outside home, but about 440 MB of plugins still sit in
  `~/.local/share` (nvim lazy 220 MB, mason 171 MB, parsers 26 MB, zinit 20 MB, tmux 3.5 MB). Wiping home
  means re-downloading and rebuilding all of it before the editor and shell work fully again.
- **Folder**: `/opt/archminimal/plugins/{nvim,zinit,tmux}`, inside the user-owned `0700` folder from 0007,
  next to the repos; not a repo itself. Same path on macOS. Created by the tools on first use; the
  folder itself by `setup repos` (0007).
- **Path in one place**: the zsh repo exports `ARCHMINIMAL_PLUGINS=/opt/archminimal/plugins`
  (`conf.d/00-env.zsh`, overridable from the environment; `local.zsh` loads too late); the others fall back to that path when it is unset
  (nvim started outside zsh, tmux server started by the desktop).
- **zsh** (`conf.d/20-plugins.zsh`): `ZINIT[HOME_DIR]=$ARCHMINIMAL_PLUGINS/zinit`.
- **tmux** (`conf/plugins.conf`): `TMUX_PLUGIN_MANAGER_PATH` = `…/plugins/tmux/`; the tpm bootstrap
  clones there.
- **nvim**: `lua/config/lazy.lua` lazy `root` and `rocks.root` = `…/plugins/nvim/lazy`, `…/lazy-rocks`;
  mason `install_root_dir` = `…/plugins/nvim/mason`; nvim-treesitter (`main`) `install_dir` =
  `…/plugins/nvim/site` (added to `runtimepath`); the molten Python host (`python-host`, Makefile
  `notebook` target and `g:python3_host_prog`) = `…/plugins/nvim/python-host`. `lazy-lock.json` stays in
  the repo; lazy's small state files and `rplugin.vim` stay in `~/.local/{share,state}/nvim` and are rebuilt.
- **Migration**: `setup migrate` gains a step: moves each existing folder (`~/.local/share/nvim/{lazy,
  mason,site}`, `~/.local/share/zinit`, `~/.local/share/tmux/plugins`) to its new place if the target
  doesn't exist, and rewrites mason's links and command wrappers, which name the old folder. The python
  host and lazy's Lua rocks have the old path built in (venv scripts, compiled luarocks paths), so they
  are rebuilt in the new place (`make notebook`, `make sync`): a small download, the rest is reused. Run after pulling the zsh, tmux and
  nvim changes; open a new terminal and restart nvim and tmux after.
- **Stays in home** (deliberately): caches (`~/.cache/zsh`, nvim swap / undo / shada), and personal
  data that is not a plugin (atuin history, `~/.ssh`, `secrets.zsh`, `local.zsh`, `~/.config/hypr/local.lua`).
  Caches rebuild themselves; personal data is a separate decision (see below).
- **Order**: zsh (exports the path) → tmux, nvim → this repo (migration + docs); one PR each, each
  referencing this ADR.
- **Consequences**: + home holds only links, caches and personal data; nothing in it needs a download to
  rebuild. − four repos carry the path; a tool updated to a new plugin location default needs its
  setting checked; nvim needs four settings instead of one, since Neovim has no per-app data dir short of
  changing `XDG_DATA_HOME`.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: zinit, tpm, lazy.nvim, mason.nvim, nvim-treesitter (`main`), uv (python host).
- Alternatives: `XDG_DATA_HOME=/opt/archminimal/…` for everything: moves every app's personal data
  (atuin history, keyrings) out of home too; a link `~/.local/share/nvim` → `/opt/…`: works, but the link
  is lost with home and plugins are not found until `make install` runs again.
